{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "game": "hsr",
  "id": "golden-scapegoat-s-mutterings",
  "name": "Golden Scapegoat's Mutterings",
  "sourceUrl": "https://honkai-star-rail.fandom.com/wiki/Golden_Scapegoat%27s_Mutterings",
  "scrapedAt": "2026-08-07T08:04:06.206Z",
  "volumes": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "volumeKey": "part-one",
      "label": "Part One",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "1"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Bundle dried fennel branches tightly, then let it fully soak in olive oil — that is how a handy torch is made."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Growth, decay, and sprouting once more... They were once unrelated to the civilized world, yet given a name by the unreasonable, and then burned to ashes again."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Like that stele amid wild brush commemorating ."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "There must always be a lamb framed for sin in this world, the traveler thought as such:"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Fire and light are the embodiment of that sin."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-68596c76efb2fa95"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A feeble flame. Its light is akin to a young girl's long hair, shimmering with silken splendor, yet destined to be devoured by the endless ."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "People always say that light and dark are opposite elements — as if they were twin sisters."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "But their natures can't be more different: Darkness is infinite time and space, clumsy and dull. Light is ephemeral life, fleeting in its brilliance."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Nameless dark clouds forever linger at the corners of the ranch. The smart lamb will persuade itself:"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"I know nothing of the butcher's knife, after all.\""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-c6eab1adb6265a63"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The sky has crossed the great sea, the storm stirring crashing waves against the coast."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Broken ivory rocks are strewn over the black reef, like lichen grown out of salt: Those are vestiges of dismembered tides."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The rides the waves with their lamb in tow. Those waves are more alabaster and more fledgling than wool..."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "and also even closer to voiceless eternity."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-75ac8ab0009f0fa8"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "4"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "One can imagine a bird's warble by picking up a feather. Therefore a feather is a singing bird."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "One can imagine a dolium's figure by picking up a ceramic shard. Therefore, a ceramic shard is a dolium, and can similarly be filled with nectar."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "One can imagine a traveler's home by seeing them. Therefore, a traveler is their home, where one can touch the rainbow speaking at the ranch."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Gods wish to see the world: Thus came ."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-ab6c87a48945d58d"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "volumeKey": "part-two",
      "label": "Part Two",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "5"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The dead live on, his bones burning."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The black tide, declaring war on the white rooftop. His home is like a decaying fig, its intact skin hiding festering pustules beneath."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The visage lost, the blood lost, the soul lost... All becomes a haze of chaos because of the regression of light. What is finally lost is the name."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "All has ground to a halt, and all has to stop."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The must die, even if the sin was ."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-90436185a0bfee6d"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "6"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The hometown's boat drifts on the water surface — this wailing wood is blistering with green foam."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "One who has never ventured far, leaving a place marked as his grave from birth, wandering across the sickly world."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "His words verge on madness, his howls like a wind-weathered statue — mute and unspoken."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-c2679f8ff3f55412"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "7"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The ebony tide, leaving nameless water on the rocks. Absolute water of reality, the water of death — thus, bearing no name."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Those who don't drink this water will die of thirst in it. Those who do will lose their own names."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "In this water that does not reflect one's face, all the world's faces are contained within."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "That face says, humans will re-discover their ."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-a35791df0d7e4465"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "volumeKey": "part-three",
      "label": "Part Three",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "5B"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Hate and the void devoured the . He was buried in the four corners of the world."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Gigantic rock mountains lost their weight, and became dark clouds in the sky."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The world is already upside down: Future is past, letters become curses, bricks that absorbed water reborn into soft earth."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The bird knows not what it sings, its only understanding in its own throat."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "In this silent world of creation, all life is revived."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-a6b349cc62416853"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "6B"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Before it matured, the lamb could talk to the dead."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Not music, not letters — black iron and charcoal were used to perform the seance."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The branding iron glowed red-hot in the furnace, its fuel being the past of . On the lamb's flawless skin, it wanted to leave a mark that denoted the shepherd's ."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The scar was its shadow cast upon time. From then on, the lamb could no longer commune with the dead."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-2c4d5fd6fb47dfdf"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "7B"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Cutting open the myrrh tree's bark, people harvest its valuable spices to embalm the bodies of the deceased."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Monoliths melted, sulfur rising, the earth has also been roasted into asphalt — those who wish to destroy all harvest heavenly fire from graves."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The eternal tree rages with fire, its wooden shards shattered into stars. Life is resurrected, perishes, and then returns once again in this primordial blaze."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The sky is a slab of lapis lazuli — before it was solidified, the lands once hurled it high into the air."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-f7446391d20989c9"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "volumeKey": "part-four",
      "label": "Part Four",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "8"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The two gods brush past each other by the shoulder along the bridge — he imagines such a scene."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "One is the blinding light that rises from infinite void, and the other is blackened blood coursing along parched earth."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "One dons a flaming crown while prostrating, and the other weeping tears of sulfur amidst hymns."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"This happened a thousand years ago\" — the elder he imagines says to the children."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Words became flesh."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-f08317346b6ecd45"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "9"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The swallows the faint light behind bars, the prison so dark he can't see past his own hand."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "He doesn't remember who locked him up here. A trail of black ants crawls past his black garb in darkness."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The lamb's skull murmurs to itself: If we had fangs and claws, you wouldn't be locked in here now."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Enough,\" he musters in a moldered voice from the depths of his corroded throat, \"the sky is but an abyss darker than a prison.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"You and I are nothing more than slaves to a distant dream.\""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-d06a690f2292f752"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "10"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The sinner was once gardener to an epitaph. The world was still young then, and the final words of the deceased had also just opened their eyes."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"The night uses its tide to cover us, the reciprocal light being its rhythm.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Sunlight wavers between movement and stoppage. That transparent flash was also once someone's life.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The dream is everything that the dream forgot."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "People are shadows of people's words."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-d59b417b32d5a789"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "11"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The sinner and the lamb are like two shredded pieces of paper: Torn apart by dreams of day, bound together in blood by dark of night. Destroyed before it all begins, living in shame after it all ends."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Letters have long been etched into eternity — that fate was, is, and will be written by the sinner's own sword, dipped in blood-ink."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The one who carries out the sacrifice is also part of the sacrificial offering."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "They all no longer have faces."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "They all no longer have names."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-f0c2346c457e3462"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "volumeKey": "part-five",
      "label": "Part Five",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "12"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The hour hand greets the minute hand's thirteenth return, just as it did the first time. The sinner cannot tell beginning and end apart."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Yesterday, I was going to tend to the flock in the sky, blanketed by white clouds, where my lambs would only be revealed when gales billowed.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Tomorrow, I will have etched fire to the slate, tempered shattered shackles with it, and forged crowns of triumph for heroes.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"And today, I will never lose my own Coreflame.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The dead have not passed, just as the living are yet to be born."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-9b4226c5a0675f57"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "13"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The waterfall bleeds the mountains, like a lamb's throat being slit. This world's evils are all the sins the traveler ."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Thus, they will ."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"We brought light to the world.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"We brought destruction to the world.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "He is alone, yet murmurs to no one."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The 's face is blurred. The 's figure overlaps."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The sky the shadow after the land's death."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-6be4c42be477dde4"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "14"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "He once brought light to the world, but now dwells in a paradise no wider than a foot."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "An obsidian urn containing ashen remains."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "He is the living dead, as well as a dead mortal. He speaks to the sky in the language of stones, and to the land in the language of fire."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "He speaks to people in the language of blood."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\" .\""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-8868db1e13aab93c"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "15"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"To think, that I can still think.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The was also surprised by himself. have taught him all languages, but he has also lost his own language."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Humans are an anomaly, for only they possess the light, and only they are deemed worthy of being slain. is indeed the great evil that he brought unto this world. As punishment, his reason, spark, or whatever this is called... has long been stripped away like a peeled onion, dismembered piece by piece."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "It's just..."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"To think, that can still think.\""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-91996a78eab45b58"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "volumeKey": "part-six",
      "label": "Part Six",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "16"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The avalanche once came."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "He is a diligent dinghy, drifting along the frozen waterfall, pursuing that carved into his soul."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "He travels against the light, for he remembers that he hasn't placed the firelight that brightens the world on its zenith. He recites his desires with blood, for the air on that zenith is so thin it suffocates — only the language of blood can leave traces in thoughts."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"I am the shepherd.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The golden fleece in the dream slumbers in the sanguine seabed."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-cfa1b01fa4ca470b"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "16B"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Too many people die too late, yet some die too soon."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The lamb says that death is a major affair as worthy of import as the most grandiose festival. Festivals won't just happen once, but death cannot be rewound."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"But you have already stepped on the altar countless times. I am the after all, so I know it well.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"That wasn't me. Seriously, it wasn't.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Don't pretend to be so relaxed.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"You're right. Sorry.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "To deliver the , killed ourselves every time."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-92b481277a631f63"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
